  "body": "Porting from https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26024. Although per https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/480 it appears the drag and drop spec in question might not be implemented anywhere, which is a separate issue?\r\n\r\nThe summary of that issue is that when you drag and drop a responsive image (i.e. one whose URL is controlled by srcset or picture) the resulting URL that gets dropped should ideally be that of the image being displayed. Whereas currently https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#drag-and-drop-processing-model just uses the src=\"\" attribute.",
